        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>Toggle and group buttons are native buttons drawn by <code>ButtonControl</code>: Tab reaches each one, Enter and Space press it, and <code>aria-pressed</code> reads "true" or "false".</li>
            <li>A button group is a <code>role="group"</code> named by <code>AriaLabel</code> ("Button group" by default); set it to say what the group chooses.</li>
            <li>Inside a button group, the arrow keys, Home and End move focus between the enabled buttons, and the arrow keys wrap at either end.</li>
            <li><code>SegmentedControl</code> is a <code>role="radiogroup"</code> of native radio inputs named by <code>AriaLabel</code> ("Segments" by default): one Tab stop, and the arrow keys move the choice. Each segment's label is its <code>Text</code>.</li>
            <li>Name an icon-only toggle with <code>aria-label</code> as well as <code>Title</code>, and give every group item visible <code>Text</code>, which names its button.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Plain and dropdown buttons: <a href="demo/buttons">Buttons</a>. A default action with alternatives: <a href="demo/split-button">Split button</a>.</li>
            <li>A labeled on/off setting, and the radio group under <code>SegmentedControl</code>: <code>SwitchControl</code> and <code>RadioGroupControl</code> in <a href="demo/checks">Checks &amp; switches</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

